 The candidate control reads both timestamps from the same inspect response and moves the second scheduling observation to a separate transaction on the 1000 ms runtime. The 60 ms runtime serves only the explicit cleanup dispatch. Missing metadata with absent/expired status prints `scheduled=fired-before-inspect`; a present invalid schedule still fails. This label includes inspect-triggered expiry purging and does not independently prove automatic alarm execution. `W1_1_OIDC_CLEANUP_INSPECT_DELAY_MS` is test-only; the normal harness forbidden string remains unchanged. None of the other six checks asserts an alarm timestamp on a short-expiry runtime.
 
 Validation remains open: Node `v22.23.2` in this worktree cannot start Miniflare because the sandbox refuses its loopback listener (`listen EPERM: operation not permitted 127.0.0.1`). The old/new delayed observations and ten baseline/ten mutant behavioral runs are not established. Local evidence and reproducible commands are recorded in `artifacts/agent-b/f177/results.md`; do not treat this candidate as a verified closure.
+
+
+### F178
+
+**The canary-budget control asserted runner timeout semantics instead of isolating our declared budget.** On 2026-09-13 the synthetic 300 ms canary / 100 ms CLI default control failed locally with Node 22.23.2: the file timed out before either subtest reported. Node 26.8.2 reported the expected subtests directly and after stripping `NODE_TEST_CONTEXT`, but inheriting that variable from a `node --test` parent suppressed the expected reporting. A clean environment did not remove the Node 22 process-isolation failure; `--experimental-test-isolation=none` did, provided the nested child did not inherit the test context. Node 22 rejects the unprefixed `--test-isolation` spelling. These observations establish version, isolation and context dependencies, not the specific historical patch that introduced them.
+
+CI run 34598579655 resolved Node **22.23.2**, on Ubuntu, at source `480da7e704b4556e298ada98d6ab6d44a53c6ee7`. Its successful job ran proof, sessions, SDK build and Docker gates; it did not run `d1:controls:test` and emitted no `D1_CANARY_BUDGET` line. The handoff's CI comparison therefore does not demonstrate this control passed. The earlier local 23-pass report alone cannot establish which historical environment differed.
+
+The replacement reads the harness default and verifies the wizard's larger declared budget is applied to its named canary test. A synthetic child without a file-level deadline observes a 40 ms per-test timeout and a passing sibling. Copied-source mutations remove the declaration or applied option, or set the declaration to the default; each must fail the same assertion and pass after restoration. This is a source-wiring and synthetic timeout control, not evidence that live Docker canary work completes within its budget. Commands, full output and repeated-run summaries are in `artifacts/agent-b/f178/`.
+
+Local verification completed ten direct and ten `npm run d1:controls:test` runs on each of Node 22.23.2 and 26.8.2. Every direct run reported 5 passed and 0 failed; every full control run reported 24 passed, 0 failed and 1 existing skip requiring Node 26.5.0. All three copied-source mutations were killed and restored in every run. These totals and each original summary line are quoted in `artifacts/agent-b/f178/all-run-summaries.log`.
